{{- /*
  blog/audience-and-tone — standard voice/audience block for the blog suite.
  A small composite that calls blog-config-fragment twice (for `audience` and
  `tone`), so consumer prompts (ideation, polish, publish, linkedin-post) can
  include one `{{ template "blog/shared/audience-and-tone" . }}` line and get:

  - the user's overrides if `{{ Arg "Folder" "blog/posts" }}/.mitto/audience.md`
    and/or `.mitto/tone.md` exist, or
  - the standard defaults ("expert practitioners, slightly informal, direct,
    no hand-holding") otherwise.

  The fragment takes no direct parameters — it forwards the caller's dot value
  to blog-config-fragment via nested dicts, and blog-config-fragment resolves
  the `Folder` argument through the caller's context. Callers must invoke this
  fragment with their own dot (`{{ template "blog/shared/audience-and-tone" . }}`).
*/ -}}
**Audience.** {{ template "blog/shared/blog-config-fragment"
  (dict "Name" "audience"
        "DefaultText" "Expert practitioners: engineers, technical leads, and hands-on architects. Assume familiarity with the domain; do not hand-hold on basics.") }}

**Tone.** {{ template "blog/shared/blog-config-fragment"
  (dict "Name" "tone"
        "DefaultText" "Slightly informal, direct, and confident. Prefer concrete examples over abstract exposition. Avoid marketing language, filler phrases, and needless qualifiers.") }}
